From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zaid <283011337+nottzaid@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Instanced shapes and visibility ranges

Shape.instancesUrl: one shape drawn at every transform of a binary
file, culled per instance and drawn with one instanced call.
Shape.visibilityRange: draw only within a camera-distance band, per
instance when instanced. Instances with a mirroring transform draw with
the front face inverted, in a second call; reverseNormals is set on
every draw, not only turned on. Passes whose programs cannot place
instances (picking, depth, stencil) skip instanced shapes instead of
drawing every instance stacked at the origin, where clicks landed.

A camera's frustum has its own dirty flag. view() rebuilt the view
matrix and cleared the flag the frustum waited on; instance culling
reads the view first, so a robot camera that had moved since its first
frame culled with its first frustum.

Replaces these patches of the numbered series, with what each measured
as it landed (tools/profile_forest.py, GTX 1060 3 GB, i5-4670):
- 0009-instancing-and-visibility-range: forest load 42 -> 20 s, frame 25
  -> 5.7 ms, RAM 3.7 -> 2.3 GB, 16,814 -> 185 geometries
- 0013-navigation-distance (its instancing part)
- 0015-mirrored-instances
- 0067-camera-frustum: without it the drone camera lost 44-83% of its
  pixels at three of five probe poses
